#
# Counter-example for math:UnframedEffectSizeShape (Rule I6): a math:EffectSize that names
# its comparison through math:effectSizeContrast and its scale through math:effectSizeScale
# (so those two arms are SATISFIED) but omits gmeow:hasReferenceFrame, tripping the frame
# arm's sh:minCount 1 — shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (math:UnframedEffectSize).
# Single violation: the contrast and scale keep their arms satisfied, so ONLY the frame
# arm fires — EXACTLY ONE finding, no sibling.
# Back-reference: math:UnframedEffectSize (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Negative counterpart of conformance-fixtures/effect-size-framed.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecEffectSizeUnframed).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:unframedD a math:EffectSize ;
    math:effectSizeContrast ex:treatmentContrast ;
    math:effectSizeScale ex:standardDeviationScale .    # contrast + scale present, but NO gmeow:hasReferenceFrame

ex:treatmentContrast a math:StatisticalContrast .
ex:standardDeviationScale a math:MeasurementScale .
